```

### Outbound: on_send Hook Architecture

Instead of a polling daemon, use rmail's `on_send` hook. This hook fires only when
a message is successfully delivered to the recipient. If the recipient is offline,
messages queue naturally in rmail's outbox until they come online.

**Key insight:** When one message successfully sends, check if there are more queued.

### Queue Storage

Game mail that needs forwarding is stored in a queue file:

```
# .pending-forwards.txt
# Format: mail_id:subscriber:character:timestamp
12345:alice:Thrall:1712345678
12346:alice:Thrall:1712345700
12347:bob:Jaina:1712345800
```

### ALE Integration: Queue on Mail Receive

When in-game mail arrives, ALE queues it for forwarding:

```lua
-- {{{ OnMailReceive hook (ALE)
-- Queue mail for rmail forwarding when it arrives in-game

local PENDING_FILE = "/mnt/mtwo/games/azeroth-core/wow-chat-2026/game-mail/mail/.pending-forwards.txt"
local SUBSCRIPTIONS_FILE = "/mnt/mtwo/games/azeroth-core/wow-chat-2026/game-mail/mail/subscriptions.txt"

local function OnMailReceive(event, receiver, mailId)
    local receiverName = receiver:GetName()
    local subscribers = getSubscribersForCharacter(receiverName)

    if #subscribers == 0 then return end

    -- Queue for each subscriber
    local f = io.open(PENDING_FILE, "a")
    if f then
        local timestamp = os.time()
        for _, subscriber in ipairs(subscribers) do
            f:write(string.format("%d:%s:%s:%d\n",
                mailId, subscriber, receiverName, timestamp))
        end
        f:close()
    end

    -- Write first message to outbox to trigger send attempt
    attemptNextForward(subscribers[1])
end
-- }}}
```

### on_send Hook: Check for More

When a message successfully sends, check if there are more pending:

```lua
#!/usr/bin/env lua
-- {{{ mail-onsend.lua
-- on_send hook - fires after successful message delivery
-- Checks if more messages are queued for this recipient

local recipient = arg[1]  -- contact that just received a message
local subject   = arg[2]
local filepath  = arg[3]  -- path to sent message

local DIR = "/mnt/mtwo/games/azeroth-core/wow-chat-2026"
local PENDING_FILE = DIR .. "/game-mail/mail/.pending-forwards.txt"
local OUTBOX_PATH = DIR .. "/game-mail/mail/outbox/"

-- Only process [WoW Mail] messages (our forwarded mail)
if not subject or not subject:match("^%[WoW Mail%]") then
    os.exit(0)
end

-- {{{ checkAndSendNext
-- Look for more pending forwards for this recipient
function checkAndSendNext(recipient)
    local pending = readPendingFile()
    local toSend = nil

    for i, entry in ipairs(pending) do
        if entry.subscriber == recipient then
            toSend = entry
            -- Remove from pending
            table.remove(pending, i)
            writePendingFile(pending)
            break
        end
    end

    if toSend then
        -- Fetch mail from game DB and write to outbox
        local mail = fetchMailFromDB(toSend.mailId)
        if mail then
            writeMailToOutbox(recipient, mail)
            -- rmail will attempt to send, triggering on_send again if successful
        end
    end
end
-- }}}

checkAndSendNext(recipient)
-- }}}
```

### on_login Hook: Flush Queue

Custom hook that runs when a player logs into the game server. Triggers a check
for any pending forwards for all online rmail recipients:

```lua
#!/usr/bin/env lua
-- {{{ mail-onlogin.lua
-- Called by ALE when player logs in
-- Attempts to flush any pending mail forwards

local DIR = "/mnt/mtwo/games/azeroth-core/wow-chat-2026"
local PENDING_FILE = DIR .. "/game-mail/mail/.pending-forwards.txt"
local OUTBOX_PATH = DIR .. "/game-mail/mail/outbox/"

-- {{{ flushPendingForwards
-- Write one message per subscriber to outbox to kick off the chain
function flushPendingForwards()
    local pending = readPendingFile()
    local attemptedSubscribers = {}

    for _, entry in ipairs(pending) do
        if not attemptedSubscribers[entry.subscriber] then
            -- Write first pending message to outbox
            local mail = fetchMailFromDB(entry.mailId)
            if mail then
                writeMailToOutbox(entry.subscriber, mail)
                attemptedSubscribers[entry.subscriber] = true
            end
        end
    end
end
-- }}}

flushPendingForwards()
-- }}}
```

### ALE: Trigger on_login Hook

```lua
